>> title: Peanut Butter Cookies
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: peanut butter, brown sugar, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> servings: 36
>> time: 30 min

Heat the #oven{} to 375°F (190°C) and line two #baking sheets{} with parchment.

Cream @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(113 g; softened) with @creamy peanut butter{1%cup}(255 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), and @light brown sugar{1/2%cup}(110 g).

>> step: beat in
Beat @egg{1%large}(50 g) and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)creamed mixture{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cup}(190 g), @baking soda{3/4%tsp}(4.5 g), @baking powder{1/2%tsp}(2.4 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Stir @&(~1)dry ingredients{} into @&(~2)batter{}.

>> step: roll into balls, press flat with a fork
Roll @&(~1)dough{} into balls and press flat in a criss-cross with a #fork{}.

Bake @&(~1)cookies{} at 375°F for ~{10%min}.
